 "notes": [
  "Every mechanical rejection was repaired and re-added (M7 display, M11 hard flag, M4 complete sentence, M5 digit in claim, M1 home_chapter 21 for s3). One id (sqs-dlq-same-account-and-region) was refused only because another miner had already added it; the other miner's fact answers the same question.",
  "Ten claims were amended (rev 2) after I saw that the claim said more than the quote: eventbridge-scheduler-cron-supports-time-zones, eventbridge-rule-infinite-loop-risk, eventbridge-dlq-is-standard-sqs-queue, eventbridge-event-dropped-after-retries-exhausted, sns-topic-private-by-default, sqs-standard-best-effort-ordering, sqs-receive-keeps-message-hidden, sqs-sse-managed-encryption-on-by-default, sns-fifo-archive-replay-fifo-topics-only, sns-fifo-replay-started-by-subscriber.",
  "Duplicates with other miners exist (for example sqs-message-timer-overrides-queue-delay and sqs-message-timer-overrides-delay-queue; sqs-fifo-no-message-timers and sqs-fifo-no-per-message-timers; sqs-long-polling-wait-time-above-zero and sqs-long-polling-wait-greater-than-zero; sqs-delay-setting-retroactive-fifo-only and sqs-delay-queue-standard-not-retroactive; sqs-dlq-max-receive-count-meaning and sqs-dlq-maxreceivecount-meaning; sqs-dlq-retention-longer-than-source-queue and sqs-dlq-retention-longer-than-source; sqs-dlq-standard-keeps-original-enqueue-timestamp and sqs-dlq-standard-enqueue-timestamp-unchanged; sqs-dlq-redrive-allow-policy-default-allow-all and sqs-dlq-redrive-allow-default-all). The registrar should keep one of each pair and supersede the other.",
  "SOURCE CONFLICT 1 (SNS raw message delivery): the SNS FAQ fact sns-faq-raw-message-delivery-only-sqs-and-http-endpoints says SQS and HTTP(S) only; the SNS guide (sns-large-payload-raw-message-delivery) lists Firehose, SQS and HTTP/S. Guide is current truth: see sns-raw-delivery-firehose-body-only.",
  "SOURCE CONFLICT 2 (SQS KMS permission for producers): sqs-key-management still says the producer needs kms:Decrypt and kms:GenerateDataKey, but the SQS documentation history row of 2024-07-24 says SendMessage no longer needs kms:Decrypt (only kms:GenerateDataKey; ReceiveMessage still needs kms:Decrypt). I added only the consumer fact (sqs-kms-consumer-needs-decrypt) and no producer fact; the decisions+changes lens should add the 2024-07-24 change from the history row.",
  "SOURCE CONFLICT 3 (EventBridge IAM role for event bus targets): eb-events-iam-roles says EventBridge bus targets do not use roles and need a resource policy; eb-cross-account says all new cross-account event bus targets created after 2023-03-02 must have an IAM role, and eb-event-bus-perms recommends always using IAM roles for bus targets. I added the cross-account fact (eventbridge-cross-account-new-bus-targets-need-iam-role) and did not add the 'bus targets do not use roles' sentence.",
  "The snapshots of eb-what-is, eb-event-bus and eb-targets now describe both buses. All EventBridge behavior facts are about the default bus and Custom Event Bus - Classic. The two Classic-versus-new comparison facts (eventbridge-classic-bus-no-ordered-delivery, eventbridge-classic-bus-does-not-retain-events) carry a note that the same table row describes the new Custom Event Bus (2026-09-24, not examinable yet).",
  "S3 facts use home chapter 21 (service s3 is owned by chapter 21); Lambda and EC2 Auto Scaling facts already existed (chapters 18 and 17) and are reused by id."
 ],
